  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **Ring law only for ring sets.** A new predicate `ring_links::rings` (`Waterline | OffsetRings`, the strategy of the posted passes) gates `ring_links::for_side` at both callers: `pocket.rs` and the plain source of `pocket_avoid.rs`.\n  - Zigzag rows round a part keep the links that they had before #3818.\n  - The 2D Pocket with Outside containment stays under the ring law (the coordinator's decision). It now has pins.\n  - 2D Adaptive is no ring set. Where the HSM plan runs its own spiral round a part (Outside with a stock outline, the air plan of #3355), the ring law does not link it, and it posts the moves of main before #3818 (pinned).\n  - Where the HSM plan cannot start on the start side (a hole wall Inside; on the dog bone also Outside), it falls back to Offset rings, and a note names the fallback. Those passes are rings. The planner joins them by the in-air law of #3747 (`level_order`), so the pass links also use the ring law. They are pinned as for the pocket.\n- **A failed ring link honours `Link::Clearance`.** In `ladder_links::pass_link`, a failed ring link lifts to `clearance_z` when the user chose Clearance for the pass link. With Retract, KeepDown or the default, it lifts to `hop_z` as before. The link tally (`links.rs`) now records the plane, and the `link:` note says \"lifted to the clearance height\" for that case. The default text does not change.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3822-pocket-ring-scope.md`.\n\n## The Adaptive pins\n\nThe brief asked for \"Adaptive Spiral output equals main before #3818\". That pin is `adaptive_spiral_round_a_part_outside_equals_main_before_3818`: the square fixture of `pocket_hsm_start_tests` with `around_part: true` and Outside, where the spiral runs (no fallback). Its digest equals the digest read on `b2ff0ef1b`, the first parent of the #3818 merge. With the predicate removed the pin is red (checked). On the dog bone, Adaptive always falls back to Offset rings, and those rings are pinned by the ring law. The Zigzag pin also equals main before #3818, and it is red without the predicate (checked).\n\n## Overlap\n\nThe #3824 worker also edits `ladder_links::pass_link`. This PR adds the `(Some(Err(why)), Link::Clearance)` arm there, which lifts to `clearance_z` and calls `tally.lift_to(.., CLEARANCE_PLANE, ..)`. The PR that merges second must keep that arm.\n\n## Pinning tests (`camcraft-motion`, `pass_start_levels::pocket_outside`)\n\n- `outside_pocket_rings_round_a_disc_do_not_lift`: Waterline and Offset rings, Inside and Outside. 0 lifts and 0 re-entries, no overcut (shape mask), no crossing feeds, each lift named.\n- `outside_pocket_dog_bone_names_each_lift`: the same laws on the #3744 dog bone.\n- `failed_ring_link_lifts_to_the_users_pass_plane`: a clamp across the link, on both ring strategies. Clearance lifts to 10.0 (clearance), and Retract and KeepDown lift to 2.0 (retract). Each lift is named, and the note names the plane.\n- `zigzag_rows_keep_their_links_round_a_part`: the digest equals main before #3818.\n- `adaptive_spiral_round_a_part_outside_equals_main_before_3818`: the Adaptive air-plan spiral round a part, Outside, equals main before #3818.\n- `adaptive_fallback_rings_link_by_the_ring_law`: the fallback is named, no overcut, no crossing, each lift named.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Rework head (after `git merge origin/main`, which includes #3823): `pass_start_levels` 19 passed; `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test pocket_pass_start` 5 passed, 2 ignored; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nFirst head:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test pass_start_levels`: 18 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 172 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (41.4 min). The plan includes `app suites: adaptive_pass_start` and `offset_pass_start`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Targeted heavy step (P1): `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: pocket_pass_start\"`: ok (874 s).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `app heavy: offset_pass_start` (fig8 Offset2D): not run. That path does not change, except for the Clearance lift plane.\n- The light lane and the example catalogs: not run.\n\nChangelog: 2D Pocket and 2D Offset round a part: a ring link that fails now lifts to the clearance height when the pass link is Clearance, and the note names that plane; Zigzag rows keep their earlier links.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3822\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
